("v733", "scalar", "Perez argues that Edamadaka et al.'s representational-alignment results independently validate Quaternion Process Theory (QPT). Claimipedia separately records the empirical paper's findings, the compatibility mapping to QPT, the stronger truth and universality extrapolations, and the presently absent quaternion-specific operational test. The essay cites a QPT formal specification as a document provided for analysis rather than a publicly recoverable primary source, so priority, frozen predictions and exact axioms remain acquisition tasks.")
