("v1008", "type", "String")
("v1008", "scalar", "The site describes Rev33.2 as a sealed 444-page suite centered on the split-octonionic exceptional Jordan algebra J3(O_s), with a source ledger, executable kernels and a 357-record registrar. It also states that the work is pre-print, not peer-reviewed, not published outside the programme, and has zero house-adjudicated records. Claimipedia admits the corpus as an ad hoc review target, not as evidence or an accepted theory. Its tier labels and internal AI reviews are preserved as first-party metadata and are not upgraded to independent validation.")
