("v2509", "type", "String")
("v2509", "scalar", "Ordinary finite-group averaging cannot supply the desired untwisted cancellation because it annihilates nontrivial irreducibles but preserves the invariant sector; any successful bridge needs a new input.")
("v2508", "value", "v2509")
("v2501", "entry", "v2510")
("v2510", "type", "Entry")
("v2510", "key", "steelman")
("v2511", "type", "String")
("v2511", "scalar", "This is the thread's most informative result. The Reynolds operator projects onto invariants, so it cannot by itself cancel a trivial or untwisted contribution. A viable route would need a signed or character-weighted trace, a nontrivial family, a trace formula with oscillatory phases, or another source of cancellation whose hypotheses are independently justified.")
("v2510", "value", "v2511")
