("v4129", "type", "String")
("v4129", "scalar", "A group action and a field structure may be two shadows of a common operator algebra: the operators commuting with an irreducible finite-group action can canonically form a finite extension field.")
("v4128", "value", "v4129")
("v4121", "entry", "v4130")
("v4130", "type", "Entry")
("v4130", "key", "steelman")
("v4131", "type", "String")
("v4131", "scalar", "For an irreducible finite-dimensional representation V over F_q, Schur's lemma makes End_G(V) a finite division ring, and Wedderburn makes that ring a finite field. Thus an independently given action can select extension-field scalar multiplication rather than merely matching a field cardinality.")
("v4130", "value", "v4131")
