("v4165", "type", "Entry")
("v4165", "key", "attributedClaim")
("v4166", "type", "String")
("v4166", "scalar", "Monster structures can undergo a mathematically meaningful field or characteristic change because the moonshine vertex operator algebra has a Monster-symmetric self-dual integral form that admits base change.")
("v4165", "value", "v4166")
("v4158", "entry", "v4167")
("v4167", "type", "Entry")
("v4167", "key", "steelman")
("v4168", "type", "String")
("v4168", "scalar", "A single integral Monster object can produce complex, p-adic and finite-characteristic representation-theoretic shadows. At primes dividing the Monster order, modular representation theory can become non-semisimple, so blocks, extensions and Tate cohomology are a precise category-changing analogue of a phase shift.")
