("v4233", "entry", "v4240")
("v4240", "type", "Entry")
("v4240", "key", "attributedClaim")
("v4241", "type", "String")
("v4241", "scalar", "Monster moonshine and Spin(2,3) meet exactly at genus two through Siegel modular geometry.")
("v4240", "value", "v4241")
("v4233", "entry", "v4242")
("v4242", "type", "Entry")
("v4242", "key", "steelman")
("v4243", "type", "String")
("v4243", "scalar", "The exact bridge is representation-theoretic, not a coordinate identification. Tuite's genus-two construction supplies a scalar Siegel numerator of weight 12. Its lowest U(2) type is (12,12)=det^12; through Sp4(R) locally isomorphic to SO(2,3), this is the positive-energy carrier D(12,0) with quadratic Casimir and AdS mass parameter 108. Post-strike controls show that this carrier is generic across sampled self-dual c=24 theories. RIO-018 v7 resolves the exact packet content: in constant/boundary-normalized Siegel, Klingen and Maass coordinates, Moonshine is (1, -82104/691, 701916528/543781), with an independent Fourier coefficient reconstructed exactly. RIO-018 v8 pins 1A/2B/7A through q^2 and proves that scalar Z(7A,1) gives only the rank-one Held row (51,51). RIO-018 v9 then finds the exact missing component in Ivanov and Tuite: the conjugate Held-7A/7B generalized-moonshine functions have first Held-7A row (-3/2+3i sqrt(7)/2, -3/2-3i sqrt(7)/2), whose determinant with the identity row is -153i sqrt(7). Thus 51a/51b are locally identifiable, provided the cyclotomic orientation is retained. RIO-018 v10 shows that the two functions have nonconjugate S4 stabilizers of index seven in PSL(2,7), so a modularly and Galois-complete boundary object requires two seven-component orbits rather than a two-component pair. The published objects are genus-one traces, not yet a genus-two Held action on W tensor D(12,0). The symmetric spaces Sp4(R)/U(2) and AdS4 remain different.")
("v4242", "value", "v4243")
("v4233", "entry", "v4244")
("v4244", "type", "Entry")
("v4244", "key", "missingMiddle")
("v4245", "type", "Sequence")
