("v5300", "key", "attributedClaim")
("v5301", "type", "String")
("v5301", "scalar", "Altaisky's continuous-wavelet formulation replaces point fields by resolution-dependent fields phi_a(x), restricts internal resolutions relative to external detector resolution, and can render perturbative Green functions finite while expressing renormalization as scale dependence.")
("v5300", "value", "v5301")
("v5293", "entry", "v5302")
("v5302", "type", "Entry")
("v5302", "key", "steelman")
("v5303", "type", "String")
("v5303", "scalar", "Continuous wavelets can supply a covariant multiresolution representation and an explicit operational scale label. If the admissible-wavelet measure, locality properties and gauge identities are controlled, this may be a useful regulator or effective-field representation whose detector resolution is visible rather than hidden behind a cutoff.")
("v5302", "value", "v5303")
