("v5604", "type", "String")
("v5604", "scalar", "Hofstadter band widths and gaps receive calculable instanton corrections whose multi-instanton ambiguities cancel divergent perturbative ambiguities, yielding a resurgent completion of spectral self-similarity.")
("v5603", "value", "v5604")
("v5596", "entry", "v5605")
("v5605", "type", "Entry")
("v5605", "key", "steelman")
("v5606", "type", "String")
("v5606", "scalar", "Semiclassical instantons and resurgence can encode exponentially small spectral splittings invisible to ordinary perturbation theory. The Hofstadter problem is attractive because these predictions can be compared directly with high-precision lattice spectra rather than inferred from analogy.")
