("v6306", "key", "steelman")
("v6307", "type", "String")
("v6307", "scalar", "Agreement among independently successful models can be evidence that they capture task-relevant invariants of a shared physical domain. It is not sufficient for truth: models can share data leakage, labels, inductive biases, misspecification or a common low-information collapse. Truth requires external calibration and intervention, not agreement alone.")
